.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt DISKCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm diskctl
.Nd reread a disk's partition table, print its identity, move its backup table or type its EFI system partition
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm reread Ar DEVICE
.Nm
.Cm id Ar DEVICE
.Nm
.Cm relocate Ar DEVICE
.Nm
.Cm esp Ar DEVICE
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command rereads a disk's partition table, prints the identity the boot
command line names the disk by, moves a GUID table's backup to the
disk's last sectors, or gives an MBR's first entry the EFI system
partition's type.
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm reread Ar DEVICE
Issue
.Dv BLKRRPART
on the whole-disk node
.Ar DEVICE
to create nodes for partitions just written by a program.
The kernel refuses the request with
.Er EBUSY
while a file system on the disk is mounted or another descriptor is open
on the disk.
This prevents a reread from changing the partition bounds used by a
mounted file system.
.It Cm id Ar DEVICE
Print the disk's identity.
On an MBR disk it is the MBR signature, the four bytes at offset 440 in
the first sector, as eight lowercase hexadecimal digits.
On a disk whose first sector is a protective MBR, it is the GUID table's
disk GUID in its 36-character text form, read from the primary header
when the header and its entry array pass their checksums, and otherwise
from the backup at the disk's last sector.
.Xr growroot 8
and the boot command line use it, as
.Ql MBRID=ID,N
or
.Ql GPTID=GUID,N .
.It Cm relocate Ar DEVICE
Move a GUID table's backup to the disk's last 33 sectors and rewrite both
copies with their checksums.
A disk image written to a larger disk leaves its backup where the image
ended, and a reader looks for it at the disk's end.
A table whose primary header or array does not check is read from the
backup, and the primary is written again from it; GRUB's BIOS core reads
no backup, so a disk in that state boots by BIOS only after this, or after
UEFI firmware built on EDK2 has read it, which writes the primary itself.
The last usable sector becomes the one before the backup entry array, and
the protective MBR's entry is made to cover the disk, with the boot code
around it kept.
The backup array and header are written first and the primary array and
header after them, so that after any part of the writes one copy passes
its checksums; when only the backup passed, the primary is written first,
for the same reason.
A table whose entry size is not a multiple of 128 bytes, which the kernel
refuses, is not read from that copy.
The kernel then reads the table again as
.Cm reread
does.
The size of the disk is the kernel's, from
.Pa /proc/disk .
Writing a whole-disk node requires the recovery kernel.
.It Cm esp Ar DEVICE
Give entry 1 of the disk's MBR the type 0xEF, which UEFI firmware boots
from on an MBR disk, and read the table again as
.Cm reread
does.
The entry must have a FAT type already, 0x0B or 0x0C, or have 0xEF, which
is left as it is; a GUID table's protective MBR is refused.
The table is read again in either case, so that a run whose reread was
refused, after it wrote the type, is finished by the next one.
This is the last step of
.Ql rach2-install --update
converting an MBR disk to boot by UEFI as well, after it has made the
boot partition's file system one UEFI firmware reads.
Writing a whole-disk node requires the recovery kernel.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl diskctl id /dev/disk0
.Dl diskctl relocate /dev/disk0
.Pp
The installer uses all four commands.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
An invalid command or operand count prints:
.Dl usage: diskctl reread DEVICE | diskctl id DEVICE | diskctl relocate DEVICE | diskctl esp DEVICE
Diagnostics identify the device.
A reread refused with
.Er EBUSY
prints:
.Dl diskctl: DEVICE is in use: unmount everything on it and close every program holding it
A completed relocation prints:
.Dl diskctl: result: DEVICE: the backup table was moved to sectors FIRST to LAST
or, when the backup was already there,
.Ql is in
in place of
.Ql was moved to ,
and, when the primary was written again from the backup:
.Dl diskctl: result: DEVICE: the primary table was written again from the backup, which is in sectors FIRST to LAST
Refusals of
.Cm relocate
include
.Ql its GUID table does not read or check ,
.Ql has an MBR and no GUID table ,
.Ql the whole-disk node does not reach the disk's last sector
and
.Ql a partition reaches past where the backup table would go .
.Cm esp
prints
.Ql diskctl: result: DEVICE: entry 1 is the EFI system partition, type 0xef
and refuses a disk with
.Ql has a GUID table, whose entries have no type byte
or
.Ql entry 1 has type 0xNN, which is not a FAT one .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr disk 7 ,
.Xr growroot 8 ,
.Xr rach2-install 8
